Subject: [PATCH] esp32/p4: enable the OV5647 sensor driver for every P4 variant

cameraif's own micropython.cmake says the sdkconfig options are what matter
and that they live in the cameraif patch -- and they did not live anywhere.
No fragment in this tree set CONFIG_CAMERA_OV5647, so the only P4 image that
ever had a working camera was a build directory whose sdkconfig had been set
by hand on 2026-09-07 (build-ESP32_GENERIC_P4-C6_WIFI). Every fresh build,
and every other variant -- including the PRE_REV3_C6_WIFI one the Waveshare
panel needs -- shipped cameraif with an empty sensor-detect array.

What that costs is a wiring-shaped error for a build-configuration cause:
esp_cam_sensor drivers register through a linker section, so with no driver
compiled the array is empty and cameraif reports "no camera sensor answered
on SCCB" on a perfectly good bus. The note in micropython.cmake was written
about exactly this and could not prevent it, because nothing carried the
options.

A fragment on the P4 common config rather than on one variant, because the
CSI controller is a property of the chip, not of which radio is attached.

diff --git a/ports/esp32/boards/mpconfigboard_esp32p4_common.cmake b/ports/esp32/boards/mpconfigboard_esp32p4_common.cmake
--- a/ports/esp32/boards/mpconfigboard_esp32p4_common.cmake
+++ b/ports/esp32/boards/mpconfigboard_esp32p4_common.cmake
@@ -3,4 +3,5 @@
 set(SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS
     boards/sdkconfig.base
     boards/sdkconfig.p4
+    boards/sdkconfig.p4_camera
 )
diff --git a/ports/esp32/boards/sdkconfig.p4_camera b/ports/esp32/boards/sdkconfig.p4_camera
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ports/esp32/boards/sdkconfig.p4_camera
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# cameraif: the MIPI-CSI sensor drivers.
+#
+# Both options are load-bearing and neither implies the other. Without
+# CONFIG_CAMERA_OV5647 the driver is not compiled at all; without the
+# AUTO_DETECT option esp_cam_sensor does not emit the `-u` that keeps its
+# detect function against --gc-sections. Either one missing leaves the
+# detect array empty, and cameraif then reports every camera as absent with
+# an SCCB error -- see cameraif/micropython.cmake, which explains why adding
+# the `-u` on the cameraif side instead does not work.
+CONFIG_CAMERA_OV5647=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_OV5647_AUTO_DETECT_MIPI_INTERFACE_SENSOR=y
